\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 1. Mentor Evidence Protection\b0\fs24\par
\pard\b Current deployed definition\b0\par
\pard\f1\fs20 CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.protect_mentor_application_skill_changes()\par
RETURNS TRIGGER\par
LANGUAGE plpgsql\par
SECURITY DEFINER\par
SET search_path = public\par
AS $$\par
BEGIN\par
  IF public.is_admin() THEN\par
    RETURN NEW;\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.status = 'verified' THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Verified mentor skill evidence cannot be changed by an applicant';\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.application_id IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.application_id\par
    OR OLD.skill_id IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.skill_id\par
    OR OLD.created_at IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.created_at THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Only an administrator can move mentor skill records';\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.status IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.status AND NEW.status <> 'pending' THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Only an administrator can review mentor skill evidence';\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.feedback IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.feedback\par
    OR OLD.reviewed_at IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.reviewed_at THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Only an administrator can change mentor skill review fields';\par
  END IF;\par
  RETURN NEW;\par
END;\par
$$;\par
\pard\f0\fs24
The current function does not protect evidence_data or skill_name. The applicant update policy therefore permits evidence modification after submission.\par
\pard\b Proposed corrected definition\b0\par
\pard\f1\fs20 CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.protect_mentor_application_skill_changes()\par
RETURNS TRIGGER\par
LANGUAGE plpgsql\par
SECURITY DEFINER\par
SET search_path = public, pg_temp\par
AS $$\par
DECLARE\par
  application_status text;\par
BEGIN\par
  IF public.is_admin() THEN RETURN NEW; END IF;\par
  IF OLD.application_id IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.application_id\par
    OR OLD.skill_id IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.skill_id\par
    OR OLD.skill_name IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.skill_name\par
    OR OLD.created_at IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.created_at THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Only an administrator can change mentor skill identity';\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.feedback IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.feedback\par
    OR OLD.reviewed_at IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.reviewed_at THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Only an administrator can change mentor skill review fields';\par
  END IF;\par
  SELECT ma.status INTO application_status\par
  FROM public.mentor_applications AS ma\par
  WHERE ma.id = OLD.application_id AND ma.user_id = auth.uid();\par
  IF application_status IS NULL THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Mentor application ownership could not be verified';\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.status = 'verified' THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Verified mentor skill evidence cannot be changed by an applicant';\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.status IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.status AND NOT (\par
    (application_status IN ('not_applied', 'verification_failed') AND NEW.status = 'pending')\par
    OR (application_status = 'pending_verification'\par
        AND OLD.status = 'needs-evidence' AND NEW.status = 'pending')\par
  ) THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Invalid applicant skill status transition';\par
  END IF;\par
  IF OLD.evidence_data IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.evidence_data AND NOT (\par
    application_status IN ('not_applied', 'verification_failed')\par
    OR (application_status = 'pending_verification' AND OLD.status = 'needs-evidence')\par
  ) THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Mentor evidence is immutable after submission';\par
  END IF;\par
  RETURN NEW;\par
END;\par
$$;\par
\pard\f0\fs24
Administrators remain authorized because the first branch returns NEW for public.is_admin(). RLS and the administrator check continue to control who can reach the update.\par
\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 2. Mentor Approval\b0\fs24\par
\pard\b Current deployed definition\b0\par
\pard\f1\fs20 CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.admin_approve_mentor_application(application_id UUID)\par
RETURNS VOID LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER SET search_path = public AS $$\par
DECLARE applicant_id UUID;\par
BEGIN\par
  IF NOT public.is_admin() THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Administrator access required'; END IF;\par
  SELECT user_id INTO applicant_id\par
  FROM public.mentor_applications\par
  WHERE id = application_id AND competency_verified = true AND status <> 'suspended'\par
  FOR UPDATE;\par
  IF applicant_id IS NULL THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Application not found or competency verification has not passed';\par
  END IF;\par
  UPDATE public.mentor_applications\par
  SET status = 'approved', admin_approved = true,\par
      approved_at = timezone('utc'::text, now()),\par
      reviewed_by = auth.uid(), updated_at = timezone('utc'::text, now())\par
  WHERE id = application_id;\par
  UPDATE public.profiles SET role = 'mentor', updated_at = timezone('utc'::text, now())\par
  WHERE id = applicant_id;\par
END;\par
$$;\par
\pard\f0\fs24
The current function checks administrator authorization and competency verification, but not identity verification or the required pending_admin_approval status.\par
\pard\b Proposed corrected definition\b0\par
\pard\f1\fs20 CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.admin_approve_mentor_application(application_id UUID)\par
RETURNS VOID LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER SET search_path = public, pg_temp AS $$\par
DECLARE applicant_id UUID;\par
BEGIN\par
  IF auth.uid() IS NULL OR NOT public.is_admin() THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Administrator access required';\par
  END IF;\par
  SELECT ma.user_id INTO applicant_id\par
  FROM public.mentor_applications AS ma\par
  WHERE ma.id = admin_approve_mentor_application.application_id\par
    AND ma.status = 'pending_admin_approval'\par
    AND ma.identity_verified = true\par
    AND ma.competency_verified = true\par
    AND ma.admin_approved = false\par
  FOR UPDATE;\par
  IF applicant_id IS NULL THEN\par
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Application is not eligible for administrator approval';\par
  END IF;\par
  UPDATE public.mentor_applications\par
  SET status = 'approved', admin_approved = true,\par
      approved_at = timezone('utc'::text, now()), reviewed_by = auth.uid(),\par
      updated_at = timezone('utc'::text, now())\par
  WHERE id = admin_approve_mentor_application.application_id\par
    AND status = 'pending_admin_approval'\par
    AND identity_verified = true AND competency_verified = true\par
    AND admin_approved = false;\par
  IF NOT FOUND THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Application approval update failed'; END IF;\par
  UPDATE public.profiles SET role = 'mentor', updated_at = timezone('utc'::text, now())\par
  WHERE id = applicant_id;\par
END;\par
$$;\par
\pard\f0\fs24
\pard\b\fs28 3. Database Grants\b0\fs24\par
\pard
Current production grants include broad ALL privileges for anon and authenticated on mentor_application_skills, mentor_applications, mentor_verification_history, and profiles. Important RPCs also have broad grants to anon, authenticated, and service_role.\par
\pard
Proposed grants:\par
\pard\li360
profiles: anon none; authenticated SELECT; service_role ALL.\par
mentor_applications: anon none; authenticated SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE; service_role ALL.\par
mentor_application_skills: anon none; authenticated SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE; service_role ALL.\par
mentor_verification_history: anon none; authenticated SELECT; service_role ALL.\par
submit_mentor_application(uuid): authenticated EXECUTE only.\par
admin_approve_mentor_application(uuid): authenticated EXECUTE only.\par
is_admin(): authenticated EXECUTE only.\par
Trigger and event-trigger functions: no client grants.\par
\pard\li0
These permissions preserve all inspected application operations. No inspected browser call site requires client-side deletes on the application tables or direct profile insertion.\par
\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 4. Migration Baseline\b0\fs24\par
Production contains application objects but reports empty migration history. The baseline will be generated from the verified live application-owned schema, excluding managed Auth and Storage internals.\par
\pard\li360
1. Capture and review the live schema.\par
2. Create a baseline migration locally for application-owned objects only.\par
3. Validate it on a fresh local database and a local database with representative existing rows.\par
4. Compare columns, constraints, functions, triggers, policies, and grants with production.\par
5. Mark the baseline as applied in production using migration history repair, rather than replaying its DDL.\par
6. Apply all later migrations normally and individually.\par
\pard\li0
The proposed sequence is:\par
\pard\li360\f1\fs20
20261118000000_baseline_public_schema.sql\par
20261118000001_harden_mentor_skill_immutability.sql\par
20261118000002_require_identity_for_mentor_approval.sql\par
20261118000003_harden_public_grants.sql\par
20261118000004_align_profile_name_mapping.sql\par
20261118000005_configure_avatar_storage.sql\par
20261118000006_configure_private_mentor_verification_storage.sql\par
\pard\f0\fs24\li0
Existing rows are preserved because the baseline is not replayed against production, migration repair changes history only, and later migrations contain no unreviewed destructive operations.\par
\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 5. Profile and Avatar Compatibility\b0\fs24\par
Use production's existing full_name column as canonical. Change application queries from profiles.name to profiles.full_name and map full_name to the existing UI name field. Do not rename the production column.\par
\pard
Keep avatar_url in Auth user_metadata. Do not add profiles.avatar_url solely for this issue. Create the missing avatars bucket and preserve existing Auth metadata values.\par
\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 6. Storage\b0\fs24\par
\pard\b Avatars\b0\par
Proposed configuration: public bucket named avatars, 5 MiB limit, MIME types image/jpeg, image/png, and image/webp. Public SELECT is allowed; authenticated INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE require the first path segment to equal auth.uid(). Anonymous upload, update, and delete are not allowed.\par
\pard\b Private mentor-verification\b0\par
Proposed configuration: private bucket named mentor-verification, 10 MiB limit, MIME types application/pdf, image/jpeg, image/png, and image/webp. Paths use user_id/application_id/document_id.\par
Applicants may upload and read only their own application evidence. Administrators may read, update, and delete evidence through public.is_admin(). Anonymous users have no access. Private reads use short-lived signed URLs.\par
\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 7. localStorage Scope\b0\fs24\par
The initial security-hardening implementation will not rewrite the localStorage data layer. It will address database integrity, RLS, grants, Storage, migration baseline, profile compatibility, and tests. Moving sessions, workshops, roadmaps, notifications, recommendations, and profiles to Supabase is deferred to a separate architectural phase.\par
\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 8. Testing and Rollback\b0\fs24\par
Local fixtures will contain learner, pending, verification-failed, pending-admin-approval, approved, rejected, and suspended applications, plus pending, needs-evidence, and verified skill rows.\par
Every migration will be tested against a fresh local database and a local database containing representative existing rows. Tests will verify RLS, unauthorized updates, privilege escalation, status transitions, Storage ownership, Auth behavior, constraints, and data preservation.\par
Deployment will stop on any unexpected authorization success/failure, schema mismatch, policy omission, or data change. A production backup is required before deployment. Failed migrations will use transactional rollback where possible, otherwise a reviewed forward fix or backup restoration.\par
\pard\par
\pard\b\fs28 9. Revised Implementation Order\b0\fs24\par
\pard\li360
1. Critical database fixes: evidence immutability and approval prerequisites.\par
2. Mentor workflow: valid status transitions and verification history.\par
3. RLS and grants: least-privilege table and RPC permissions.\par
4. Storage: avatars and private mentor-verification buckets and policies.\par
5. Migration baseline: tracked public schema and production alignment.\par
6. Frontend compatibility: full_name mapping, avatar integration, and lint fixes.\par
7. Future architecture: move authoritative domain data out of localStorage and implement secure account deletion.\par
\pard\li0
\pard\b Stage 2 has not started. Explicit approval is required before implementation.\b0\par
